  "fidelityReview": {
    "target": "medium-fi",
    "status": "passed",
    "inputHash": "sha256:0f5e206db1c9a1bad78780f2f0436ea819db8aa4fea0411c9887f1f6d4f6200f",
    "notes": "The four façades, glazed entrance leaves, continuous soffit, curved red hip and six roof gables resolve the rectangular station. The entrance proportions and rooftop equipment are interpretations of the retained photographs. The local visualization grade removes high urban returns in the global Terrarium data. The exterior threshold, bed heights and roof proportions are photographic and terrain-based estimates, with a smooth transition to the host field. The modeled headhouse uses the mapped 30 m height and 18 m roof-height tags as coarse controls. The visible eaves, roof levels and communications frames are reconstructed from photos. The independent MRT entrances, bus shelters and surrounding buildings retain their map-derived geometry. Exact lettering, rooftop equipment and navigable interiors are outside this exterior model."
  },
